    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "it doesn't feel like i just need a break though. it feels more like the well is actually dead. like the person who used to create those things doesn't even exist anymore. it's just me sitting here in the quiet, waiting for something that's never coming back. it feels so pointless to just keep going through the motions when the core of me is gone.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That profound sense of loss—where even the memory of your former self feels like a stranger—can be more like a grief than a simple tiredness. It's okay to sit with that quiet and let it be what it is, without forcing a resurrection. Sometimes the \"old\" you isn't gone, but buried under layers of expectation and pressure that need to be gently excavated. You don't have to create today; just surviving this hollow space is enough.",
      "source": "target",
